</span><span class="ͼm">st</span><span class="ͼg">.</span><span>dataframe(</span><span class="ͼm">display_input</span><span>, </span><span class="ͼm">use_container_width</span><span class="ͼg">=</span><span class="ͼj">True</span><span>)</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<p dir="auto" data-start="5707" data-end="5751">and you had the <code data-start="5723" data-end="5738">display_input</code> <code data-start="5739" data-end="5750">NameError</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="5753" data-end="5999">You have now shown that the <strong data-start="5781" data-end="5833">prediction result itself is working successfully</strong>, so that issue appears to have been fixed. If the current deployed Streamlit page also works without that error, you don't need to make another change just for this.</p>
<hr data-start="6001" data-end="6004">
<h2 data-section-id="bnu6yr" dir="auto" data-start="6006" data-end="6031">Final report checklist</h2>
