/svg></div></span></button></div></div></div></div><span class="sr-only"><br></span></section></div><div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-6ab27371-ec3c-83ee-aa16-6c7d55849f79-1" data-is-intersecting="true"><section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-6ab27371-ec3c-83ee-aa16-6c7d55849f79-1" data-turn-id-container="request-6ab27371-ec3c-83ee-aa16-6c7d55849f79-1" data-testid="conversation-turn-14" data-turn="assistant"><h4 class="sr-only select-none">ChatGPT said:</h4><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div data-conversation-screenshot-content="" class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 [&amp;&gt;div:has([data-free-thinking-preview-answer=true])+:is(.text-message,.relative:has(&gt;.text-message))]:-mt-2 grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="1396ba77-ec5f-4cf3-bd19-c289d17da2d0" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-6" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="LR5Y_W_content markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full light markdown-new-styling"><p dir="auto" data-start="0" data-end="101">Yes. We should now treat this as a <strong data-start="35" data-end="69">UI/portfolio enhancement phase</strong>, not a model-development phase.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="103" data-end="361">I looked at both images. The reference has a much more polished <strong data-start="167" data-end="208">financial-risk/product dashboard feel</strong>, while your current application already has the important functionality but looks more like a basic Streamlit academic dashboard. So the goal should be:</p>
<blockquote data-start="363" data-end="574">
<p dir="auto" data-start="365" data-end="574"><strong data-start="365" data-end="574">Keep every existing calculation, model, dataset, prediction logic, charts and navigation working exactly as they are, but upgrade the visual design and add a few genuinely useful recruiter-facing features.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto" data-start="576" data-end="705">And yes — <strong data-start="586" data-end="636">I will give you prompts for IBM Bob, not code.</strong> You can paste the prompts one by one and let Bob modify the project.</p>
<h2 data-section-id="8ex74m" dir="auto" data-start="707" data-end="749">First: the design direction I recommend</h2>
<p dir="auto" data-start="751" data-end="813">Don't copy Moody's exactly. Use it only as visual inspiration.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="815" data-end="896">Your application should look like a <strong data-start="851" data-end="895">professional Loan Risk Analytics product</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="898" data-end="1254">
<li data-section-id="t98etx" data-start="898" data-end="928">
<p dir="auto" data-start="900" data-end="928">clean white/light background</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="15qicdw" data-start="929" data-end="959">
<p dir="auto" data-start="931" data-end="959">dark navy/blue primary color</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="lui22j" data-start="960" data-end="985">
<p dir="auto" data-start="962" data-end="985">subtle light-blue cards</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="j4krd0" data-start="986" data-end="1011">
<p dir="auto" data-start="988" data-end="1011">professional typography</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="xgt06k" data-start="1012" data-end="1027">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1014" data-end="1027">rounded cards</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="s595vt" data-start="1028" data-end="1048">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1030" data-end="1048">consistent spacing</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="147kr5p" data-start="1049" data-end="1065">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1051" data-end="1065">modern sidebar</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="wrul5p" data-start="1066" data-end="1077">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1068" data-end="1077">KPI cards</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="19c80ml" data-start="1078" data-end="1095">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1080" data-end="1095">section headers</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="95p1cr" data-start="1096" data-end="1121">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1098" data-end="1121">better visual hierarchy</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="187c2br" data-start="1122" data-end="1154">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1124" data-end="1154">restrained use of emojis/icons</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="qzt0tq" data-start="1155" data-end="1174">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1157" data-end="1174">responsive layout</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1hog8ns" data-start="1175" data-end="1212">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1177" data-end="1212">clear call-to-action for prediction</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="2k9a5" data-start="1213" data-end="1254">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1215" data-end="1254">professional financial/risk terminology</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto" data-start="1256" data-end="1290">Your current six pages can remain:</p>
<ol data-start="1292" data-end="1406">
<li data-section-id="10bcdvi" data-start="1292" data-end="1315">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1295" data-end="1315"><strong data-start="1295" data-end="1315">Home / Dashboard</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="5r93tm" data-start="1316" data-end="1331">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1319" data-end="1331"><strong data-start="1319" data-end="1331">Overview</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="10b1il4" data-start="1332" data-end="1342">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1335" data-end="1342"><strong data-start="1335" data-end="1342">EDA</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="15p3a32" data-start="1343" data-end="1363">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1346" data-end="1363"><strong data-start="1346" data-end="1363">Risk Analysis</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1y1y5ah" data-start="1364" data-end="1388">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1367" data-end="1388"><strong data-start="1367" data-end="1388">Model Performance</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1r7j9qg" data-start="1389" data-end="1406">
<p dir="auto" data-start="1392" data-end="1406"><strong data-start="1392" data-end="1406">Prediction</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto" data-start="1408" data-end="1470">We can improve each one without changing its underlying logic.</p>
<hr data-start="1472" data-end="1475">
<h1 data-section-id="14o92x2" dir="auto" data-start="1477" data-end="1515">PHASE 1 — Give Bob this prompt first</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="1517" data-end="1624"><strong data-start="1517" data-end="1624">Do NOT ask Bob to add features yet. First make it inspect the whole project and redesign the UI safely.</strong></p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="1626" data-end="1644">Copy this exactly:</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="1646" data-end="5482"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>I want to improve the UI/UX of my existing Loan Default Risk Analysis and Prediction Streamlit project.

IMPORTANT: This is a UI/UX redesign task first. Do NOT rewrite, remove, simplify, replace, or change any existing working data-processing logic, ML logic, calculations, model loading, prediction logic, dataset handling, charts' underlying calculations, thresholds, feature engineering, or navigation functionality.

Before making changes, inspect the entire project structure and all existing dashboard pages, including:

- dashboard/app.py
- dashboard/pages/01_overview.py
- dashboard/pages/02_eda.py
- dashboard/pages/03_risk_analysis.py
- dashboard/pages/04_model_performance.py
- dashboard/pages/05_prediction.py
- src/
- models/
- data/
- requirements.txt
- README.md
- configuration files

Understand the existing functionality before modifying anything.

The current application is functional and deployed successfully. The objective is to make it look like a professional financial risk analytics product suitable for a portfolio and recruiter demonstration.

Use the attached reference image as visual inspiration for the overall professional financial-services style, but DO NOT copy Moody's branding, logo, text, or exact design.

DESIGN DIRECTION:

- Professional financial/risk analytics dashboard
- Modern corporate appearance
- Navy/dark blue as the primary accent
- White/light neutral background
- Soft blue cards
- Subtle borders and shadows
- Rounded cards where appropriate
- Clean typography
- Strong visual hierarchy
- Consistent spacing
- Minimal and professional icons
- Avoid excessive emojis
- Avoid overly colorful or childish UI
- Keep charts visually clean and consistent
- Make the application look like a real business analytics product rather than a basic academic Streamlit project

SIDEBAR:

Redesign the sidebar/navigation so it looks professional and intentional.

Include:
- Project/application name
- Short subtitle such as "Loan Default Risk Analytics"
- IBM SkillsBuild / Data Analytics Academic Internship text where appropriate
- Clean navigation labels
- Consistent icons
- Active-page highlighting
- A small project status/information section if it can be added without affecting functionality

HOME PAGE:

Redesign the current app landing page into a professional executive dashboard.

Create:
- Strong project title
- Short one-line description explaining the purpose
- A visually attractive hero/header section
- KPI summary cards
- Feature/module cards for Overview, EDA, Risk Analysis, Model Performance and Prediction
- Dataset summary card
- Clear explanation of what the application does
- A clear call-to-action directing users to the Prediction page

Do not change any existing KPI calculations. Reuse the existing calculated values.

GLOBAL UI:

Create a consistent visual design system across all pages:
- same page background
- same card styling
- same typography hierarchy
- same border radius
- same spacing
- same section-heading style
- same accent colors
- consistent button styling
- consistent dataframe/table styling
- consistent chart presentation

IMPORTANT:
Do not break existing functionality.
Do not change model behavior.
Do not change the Random Forest model.
Do not change the deployment model.
Do not change the 0.40 decision threshold.
Do not change dataset preprocessing.
Do not change existing calculations.

If custom CSS is needed, keep it centralized and maintainable rather than duplicating large CSS blocks across pages.

Also make the layout responsive enough for normal desktop and laptop screens.

After making the UI changes, run/test the application and verify that every existing page loads successfully and that the prediction workflow still works.

Do not add speculative features yet. First complete the safe global UI redesign.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="5484" data-end="5487">
<h1 data-section-id="1v008qp" dir="auto" data-start="5489" data-end="5519">PHASE 2 — After Bob finishes</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="5521" data-end="5573"><strong data-start="5521" data-end="5573">Do not immediately give Bob another huge prompt.</strong></p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="5575" data-end="5585">First run:</p>
