<h1 data-section-id="5jmlya" dir="auto" data-start="5820" data-end="5868">PHASE 2 — Upgrade the Home/Executive Dashboard</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="5870" data-end="5929">This will make the first page much stronger for recruiters.</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="5931" data-end="8032"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>Now improve the HOME / LANDING PAGE further.

Do not change any existing data calculations or backend functionality.

Transform the landing page into an executive-style Loan Risk Analytics dashboard.

The page should immediately communicate:

1. What the project does
2. What dataset is being analyzed
3. What analytical modules are available
4. That a machine-learning model is available for prediction

Use the existing project values wherever possible.

Create a polished hero section with:

Title:
"Loan Default Risk Analytics"

Subtitle:
"Data-driven analysis and machine learning for understanding and predicting loan default risk."

Add a small professional badge/tag such as:
"IBM SkillsBuild • Data Analytics Academic Internship"

Add a concise description explaining that the application combines:
- portfolio analysis
- exploratory data analysis
- risk segmentation
- machine learning model evaluation
- individual loan default prediction

Then create a KPI row using existing calculated values, such as:
- Total Loan Records
- Total Loan Value
- Default Rate
- Defaulted Loan Value

Do NOT hard-code these values if the project already calculates them.

Then create five professional module cards:

Overview
"Portfolio KPIs and summary statistics"

EDA
"Distributions, relationships and data patterns"

Risk Analysis
"Risk segmentation and default drivers"

Model Performance
"Model metrics, ROC/PR analysis and feature importance"

Prediction
"Estimate default probability for a new loan"

Make the Prediction card visually prominent because it is the main interactive ML feature.

Add a compact "How this application works" section:

Data → Analysis → Risk Insights → Model Evaluation → Prediction

Use a clean horizontal visual flow if possible.

Add a small dataset information card:
"255,347 loan records • 17 features • Binary default target"

However, if the application calculates these values dynamically, use the actual values rather than hard-coding them.

Keep everything professional and compact. Avoid excessive text.

Do not modify any model or analytical logic.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="8034" data-end="8037">
<h1 data-section-id="1uw5h22" dir="auto" data-start="8039" data-end="8100">PHASE 3 — Make Overview look like a real business dashboard</h1>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="8102" data-end="9322"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>Now redesign the Overview page to look like a professional financial portfolio analytics dashboard.

IMPORTANT:
Do not change any existing calculations, dataframe transformations, KPI formulas, filtering logic, or chart logic.

Only improve presentation and UI.

Structure the page as:

1. Page header
"Portfolio Overview"
with a short description.

2. KPI cards
Use the existing calculated metrics and present them in polished cards.

Include the existing:
- Total Loan Value
- Defaulted Loan Value
- Default Rate
- Loan/record volume metrics if already available

3. Portfolio Default Distribution
Present the existing default distribution visualization in a clean chart card.

4. Portfolio Value / Risk summary
Use the existing visualizations and tables.

5. Segment/KPI table
Style the existing table professionally with:
- readable headers
- appropriate number formatting
