- better spacing
- aligned numerical values

Add small explanatory text under major charts where useful, explaining what the visualization represents.

Do not invent new analytical conclusions.

Do not change any existing chart calculations.

Make the page visually resemble an executive risk-monitoring dashboard.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="9324" data-end="9327">
<h1 data-section-id="fgud2y" dir="auto" data-start="9329" data-end="9349">PHASE 4 — EDA page</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="9351" data-end="9447">Your EDA page should look like an actual analytics workspace rather than a collection of charts.</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="9449" data-end="10640"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>Now redesign the EDA page while preserving every existing analysis and calculation.

Do not change the underlying pandas operations, statistical calculations, datasets, or chart data.

Create a professional structure:

Header:
"Exploratory Data Analysis"
Subtitle:
"Explore distributions, relationships and patterns across the loan portfolio."

Organize the existing charts into logical sections such as:

1. Dataset Characteristics
2. Numerical Feature Analysis
3. Categorical Feature Analysis
4. Correlation / Relationships
5. Default-related Patterns

Use clean chart cards and consistent spacing.

For existing tables:
- improve formatting
- use readable column names
- format numerical values appropriately
- avoid unnecessary index display
- make tables horizontally usable

For charts:
- maintain the existing chart types unless a visual improvement is clearly safe
- use a consistent professional color palette
- improve titles and axis labels
- remove unnecessary visual clutter
- keep legends readable

Add short explanatory captions where appropriate, but do not fabricate insights.

The goal is for a recruiter to immediately understand what each analysis is showing.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="10642" data-end="10645">
<h1 data-section-id="1t2e28a" dir="auto" data-start="10647" data-end="10677">PHASE 5 — Risk Analysis page</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="10679" data-end="10770">This is an important page because it connects data analytics with business decision-making.</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="10772" data-end="11979"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>Now redesign the Risk Analysis page as a professional credit-risk analytics dashboard.

DO NOT change any existing calculations, risk formulas, thresholds, segmentation logic, or analytical outputs.

Improve only presentation and UI.

Use this structure:

Header:
"Credit Risk Analysis"

Subtitle:
"Identify portfolio segments and characteristics associated with higher observed default risk."

Create a visual hierarchy:

1. Risk Overview
2. Risk Segmentation
3. Key Risk Drivers
4. Comparative Analysis
5. Business Interpretation

Use professional risk-tier cards if the existing project already calculates risk tiers.

For existing risk tables:
- improve formatting
- highlight important values subtly
- use appropriate percentage and currency formatting
- improve readability

For existing charts:
- use consistent styling
- improve titles
- make comparison patterns visually clear
- maintain the existing calculations

Where the project already has findings, present them as concise insight cards such as:

"Key Finding"
"Observed Pattern"
"Business Implication"

Do not create unsupported claims or new statistical conclusions.

The page should feel like a credit-risk analyst's dashboard.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="11981" data-end="11984">
<h1 data-section-id="1xyokc" dir="auto" data-start="11986" data-end="12015">PHASE 6 — Model Performance</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="12017" data-end="12099">This page is particularly important because you now have the <strong data-start="12078" data-end="12098">deployment model</strong>.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="12101" data-end="12146">Your current model-performance page contains:</p>
<ul data-start="12148" data-end="12315">
<li data-section-id="z5lca4" data-start="12148" data-end="12157">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12150" data-end="12157">ROC-AUC</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1qnfnml" data-start="12158" data-end="12177">
