</li>
<li data-section-id="yhmtun" data-start="12178" data-end="12182">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12180" data-end="12182">F1</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1fs201h" data-start="12183" data-end="12193">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12185" data-end="12193">Accuracy</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ben6u1" data-start="12194" data-end="12212">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12196" data-end="12212">Confusion Matrix</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="8fge9c" data-start="12213" data-end="12236">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12215" data-end="12236">Classification Report</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1rqtjb5" data-start="12237" data-end="12248">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12239" data-end="12248">ROC Curve</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="4cxw6p" data-start="12249" data-end="12273">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12251" data-end="12273">Precision-Recall Curve</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1w4gnhk" data-start="12274" data-end="12294">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12276" data-end="12294">Feature Importance</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="vi7cd" data-start="12295" data-end="12315">
<p dir="auto" data-start="12297" data-end="12315">Threshold Analysis</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto" data-start="12317" data-end="12340">That is already plenty.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="12342" data-end="12416">So I would <strong data-start="12353" data-end="12378">not add another model</strong> just for the sake of adding features.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="12418" data-end="12427">Give Bob:</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="12429" data-end="13852"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>Now redesign the Model Performance page into a professional machine-learning model evaluation dashboard.

CRITICAL:
Do not change the trained model, deployment model, preprocessing pipeline, test split, decision threshold, prediction probabilities, or metric calculations.

The current page already contains:

- ROC-AUC
- Average Precision
- F1
- Accuracy
- Confusion Matrix
- Classification Report
- ROC Curve
- Precision-Recall Curve
- Feature Importance
- Threshold Analysis

Keep all of these.

Improve the UI hierarchy.

At the top create a "Model Summary" section with clean metric cards:

ROC-AUC
Average Precision
F1 Score
Accuracy

Add a small model information card showing the actual deployed model configuration where available, such as:
- Random Forest
- number of trees
- max depth
- class weighting
- decision threshold

Use the actual model configuration from the loaded deployment model. Do not hard-code incorrect values.

Create clearly separated sections:

1. Model Summary
2. Confusion Matrix
3. Classification Report
4. ROC Curve
5. Precision-Recall Curve
6. Feature Importance
7. Threshold Analysis

For the threshold section, clearly explain that the project uses a 0.40 decision threshold, but do not change it.

Make the page visually polished and suitable for explaining the project during an interview.

Do not remove any existing metrics or charts.
Do not change their calculations.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="13854" data-end="13857">
<h1 data-section-id="1g53s8c" dir="auto" data-start="13859" data-end="13886">PHASE 7 — Prediction page</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="13888" data-end="13957">This is where I would add the most recruiter-friendly UI improvement.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="13959" data-end="14058">Your current prediction functionality is already working, so <strong data-start="14020" data-end="14057">do not touch its prediction logic</strong>.</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="14060" data-end="16004"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>Now redesign the Prediction page into the main interactive feature of the application.

IMPORTANT:
The prediction functionality is already working correctly. Do NOT modify:

- model loading
- input feature names
- preprocessing
- model prediction
- probability calculation
- 0.40 decision threshold
- risk-tier calculation
- prediction result logic

Only improve the UI/UX around the existing functionality.

Create a professional layout with the following structure:

HEADER

"Loan Default Risk Prediction"

Subtitle:
"Estimate the probability of loan default using the trained Random Forest model."

INPUT SECTION

Organize all existing input fields into logical groups/cards:

Borrower Profile
- Age
- Education
- Employment Type
- Marital Status
- etc.

Financial Profile
- Income
- Loan Amount
- Interest Rate
- Loan Term
- DTI Ratio

Credit Profile
- Credit Score
- Number of Credit Lines
- Months Employed

Loan / Support Information
- Loan Purpose
- Mortgage
- Dependents
- Co-signer

Use the existing input widgets and values. Do not change the underlying input names or expected data types.

Add a clear primary button:

"Predict Default Risk"

After prediction, show a prominent result card containing:

Default Probability
Prediction
Risk Tier

Keep the existing values and calculations.

Create a visually strong probability visualization/gauge using the existing probability.

Clearly display the existing 40% threshold.

Add a professional explanation:

"Predicted default probability"
"Decision threshold: 40%"
"Model classification: Default / No Default"

Do not make the result sound like a guaranteed financial decision. Make it clear that it is a model prediction.

Keep the existing "View input data submitted" section, but redesign it as a clean expandable summary card.

Make the page look like a real credit-risk assessment interface rather than a generic Streamlit form.

Do not change any prediction logic.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="16006" data-end="16009">
<h1 data-section-id="7dy065" dir="auto" data-start="16011" data-end="16057">PHASE 8 — One genuinely useful extra feature</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="16059" data-end="16160">After the UI is stable, I recommend <strong data-start="16095" data-end="16102">one</strong> additional feature rather than adding 10 random features.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="16162" data-end="16193">A good one for your project is:</p>
<h3 data-section-id="1fm0ity" dir="auto" data-start="16195" data-end="16217">"Risk Explanation"</h3>
<p dir="auto" data-start="16219" data-end="16242">After prediction, show:</p>
<blockquote data-start="16244" data-end="16286">
<p dir="auto" data-start="16246" data-end="16286"><strong data-start="16246" data-end="16286">What contributed to this prediction?</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto" data-start="16288" data-end="16326">But there is an important distinction.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="16328" data-end="16481">Your Random Forest has feature importances, but <strong data-start="16376" data-end="16480">global feature importance does not mean that a particular customer's feature caused their prediction</strong>.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="16483" data-end="16523">So don't let Bob make misleading claims.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="16525" data-end="16726">We can instead provide a <strong data-start="16550" data-end="16589">simple input-profile interpretation</strong> based on the existing prediction inputs and known model features, clearly labelled as an explanatory aid rather than causal attribution.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="16728" data-end="16735">Prompt:</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="16737" data-end="17964"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>Add one carefully designed feature to the Prediction page called:

"Risk Profile Explanation"

IMPORTANT:
Do NOT alter the prediction model or prediction result.

Do NOT claim that a feature caused an individual prediction unless the project has a valid local explanation method.

Instead, after a prediction, create a concise "Risk Profile" section that summarizes the submitted applicant inputs in a business-friendly way.

For example, organize the submitted profile into:

Credit Profile
Financial Profile
Employment Profile
Loan Profile

Then identify notable submitted characteristics using transparent rule-based descriptions only when appropriate, such as:
- relatively high debt-to-income ratio
- relatively low credit score
- relatively high loan amount
- shorter employment history

Use dataset-based or clearly defined thresholds if such thresholds already exist in the project. Otherwise, avoid inventing arbitrary thresholds.

Label this section clearly as:
"Input Profile Insights"

Add a disclaimer:
"These observations summarize the submitted inputs and should not be interpreted as causal explanations of the model prediction."

Do not modify the existing prediction probability or classification.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="17966" data-end="17969">
<h1 data-section-id="17gt1k7" dir="auto" data-start="17971" data-end="18029">PHASE 9 — Add a professional "About the Project" section</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="18031" data-end="18071">This is small but useful for recruiters.</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="18073" data-end="18997"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>Add a professional "About This Project" section accessible from the application without interfering with the existing pages.

Include:

Project:
Loan Default Risk Analysis and Prediction

Context:
IBM SkillsBuild Data Analytics Academic Internship

Dataset:
255,347 loan records and 17 features with a binary Default target.

Analytics:
- Data cleaning
- Exploratory data analysis
- Portfolio KPI analysis
- Risk segmentation
- Risk-driver analysis

Machine Learning:
Random Forest classification with preprocessing for numerical and categorical variables.

Evaluation:
- ROC-AUC
- Average Precision
- F1
- Accuracy
- Confusion Matrix
- ROC Curve
- Precision-Recall Curve
- Feature Importance
- Threshold Analysis

Deployment:
Streamlit application

Keep the information concise and professional.

Do not invent additional technologies, metrics, or project claims that are not actually present in the repository.</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="18999" data-end="19002">
<h1 data-section-id="15o0fzk" dir="auto" data-start="19004" data-end="19041">One more thing I strongly recommend</h1>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19043" data-end="19072">Your current screenshot says:</p>
<blockquote data-start="19074" data-end="19158">
<p dir="auto" data-start="19076" data-end="19158"><strong data-start="19076" data-end="19158">The predictive model is a Random Forest classifier trained on 80% of the data.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19160" data-end="19172">That's good.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19174" data-end="19302">But after the UI redesign, I want the application to make the distinction between <strong data-start="19256" data-end="19269">analytics</strong> and <strong data-start="19274" data-end="19288">prediction</strong> very obvious.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19304" data-end="19349">The overall flow should visually communicate:</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19351" data-end="19424"><strong data-start="19351" data-end="19424">DATASET → EXPLORATION → RISK INSIGHTS → MODEL EVALUATION → PREDICTION</strong></p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19426" data-end="19495">That is actually a very strong story for your Data Analytics profile.</p>
<hr data-start="19497" data-end="19500">
<h2 data-section-id="g09l5l" dir="auto" data-start="19502" data-end="19531">And don't add these things</h2>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19533" data-end="19564">I would <strong data-start="19541" data-end="19548">not</strong> ask Bob to add:</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19566" data-end="19992">❌ Login/signup<br data-start="19580" data-end="19583">
❌ User authentication<br data-start="19604" data-end="19607">
❌ Fake real-time banking data<br data-start="19636" data-end="19639">
❌ Chatbot just for decoration<br data-start="19668" data-end="19671">
❌ Random AI assistant<br data-start="19692" data-end="19695">
❌ Loan approval/rejection system<br data-start="19727" data-end="19730">
❌ Payment gateway<br data-start="19747" data-end="19750">
❌ Huge animations<br data-start="19767" data-end="19770">
❌ 10 unnecessary charts<br data-start="19793" data-end="19796">
❌ Another ML algorithm just to say "multiple models"<br data-start="19848" data-end="19851">
❌ SHAP unless Bob can implement it correctly without disturbing the existing deployment<br data-start="19938" data-end="19941">
❌ Anything that changes your existing model results</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="19994" data-end="20158">Your project is already substantial. <strong data-start="20031" data-end="20094">Presentation + clarity + one or two meaningful enhancements</strong> will make it stronger than stuffing it with unrelated features.</p>
<h3 data-section-id="vu8jg9" dir="auto" data-start="20160" data-end="20195">Most important rule for IBM Bob</h3>
<p dir="auto" data-start="20197" data-end="20263">At the beginning of <strong data-start="20217" data-end="20239">every major prompt</strong>, keep this instruction:</p>
<blockquote data-start="20265" data-end="20406">
<p dir="auto" data-start="20267" data-end="20406"><strong data-start="20267" data-end="20406">"Do not modify or break existing working functionality. Inspect the existing implementation first and make only the requested changes."</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto" data-start="20408" data-end="20440">And after <strong data-start="20418" data-end="20433">each prompt</strong>, test:</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="20442" data-end="20484"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="contents"><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-(--code-block-surface) corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl [--code-block-surface:var(--bg-elevated-secondary)] dark:[--code-block-surface:var(--composer-surface-primary)] lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1"><button type="button" class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none pointer-events-auto py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#7fccfb" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div><div class="relative"><div class="pe-11 pt-3" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative z-0 flex max-w-full"><div id="code-block-viewer" dir="ltr" class="q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼd ͼr"><div class="cm-scroller"><pre class="cm-content q9tKkq_readonly m-0"><code><span>streamlit run dashboard/app.py</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=""><div class="" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"></div></div></div></div></div></div></pre>
<p dir="auto" data-start="20486" data-end="20524">Then manually check the affected page.</p>
<p dir="auto" data-start="20526" data-end="20732" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node=""><strong data-start="20526" data-end="20569">Don't give Bob all the prompts at once.</strong> Start with <strong data-start="20581" data-end="20597">PHASE 1 only</strong>. Once Bob finishes and you show me the updated screenshot/result, we can decide the next UI change based on what it actually produced.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div aria-label="Response actions" class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none -mt-1 touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto cant-hover:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" role="group" tabindex="-1" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button type="button" class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-surface-hover rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy response" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><div class="[&amp;_svg]:h-full [&amp;_svg]:w-full icon icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M15.1006 1.78516C16.793 1.78556 18.165 3.15808 18.165 4.85059V10.8838C18.1649 12.5762 16.7929 13.9478 15.1006 13.9482H13.998V15.0508C13.9976 16.7431 12.626 18.1151 10.9336 18.1152H4.90039C3.20789 18.1152 1.83537 16.7432 1.83496 15.0508V9.01758C1.83496 7.32482 3.20764 5.95215 4.90039 5.95215H6.00195V4.85059C6.00195 3.15783 7.37463 1.78516 9.06738 1.78516H15.1006ZM4.90039 7.28223C3.94218 7.28223 3.16504 8.05936 3.16504 9.01758V15.0508C3.16544 16.0087 3.94243 16.7852 4.90039 16.7852H10.9336C11.8914 16.785 12.6676 16.0086 12.668 15.0508V9.01758C12.668 8.05945 11.8917 7.28237 10.9336 7.28223H4.90039ZM9.06738 3.11523C8.10917 3.11523 7.33203 3.89237 7.33203 4.85059V5.95215H10.9336C12.6262 5.95229 13.998 7.32491 13.998 9.01758V12.6182H15.1006C16.0584 12.6178 16.8348 11.8416 16.835 10.8838V4.85059C16.835 3.89262 16.0585 3.11564 15.1006 3.11523H9.06738Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></span></button><button type="button" class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-surface-hover rounded-lg" aria-label="Share" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><div class="[&amp;_svg]:h-full [&amp;_svg]:w-full icon icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16.6663 10.1681C17.0335 10.1681 17.3313 10.4659 17.3313 10.8332V14.1994C17.3313 15.929 15.929 17.3312 14.1995 17.3312H5.80005C4.07048 17.3312 2.66821 15.929 2.66821 14.1994V10.8332C2.66821 10.4659 2.96598 10.1681 3.33325 10.1681C3.70052 10.1681 3.99829 10.4659 3.99829 10.8332V14.1994C3.99829 15.1944 4.80502 16.0011 5.80005 16.0011H14.1995C15.1945 16.0011 16.0012 15.1944 16.0012 14.1994V10.8332C16.0012 10.466 16.2991 10.1683 16.6663 10.1681Z" fill="currentColor"></path> <path d="M9.31763 3.08317C9.71412 2.76014 10.2865 2.75993 10.6829 3.08317L10.7649 3.15739L14.012 6.40446C14.2716 6.66406 14.2714 7.08517 14.012 7.34489C13.7523 7.60459 13.3312 7.60459 13.0715 7.34489L10.6653 4.93864V11.8752C10.6653 12.2423 10.3674 12.54 10.0002 12.5402C9.63297 12.5402 9.33521 12.2424 9.33521 11.8752V4.93669L6.92896 7.34489C6.66926 7.60459 6.24725 7.60459 5.98755 7.34489C5.72836 7.08521 5.72817 6.66402 5.98755 6.40446L9.23462 3.15739L9.31763 3.08317Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></div></span></button><span class="" data-state="closed"><button type="button" id="radix-_r_1tu_" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" class="cursor-pointer touch:px-2.5 text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-surface-hover h-[30px] rounded-lg px-1.5" aria-label="Switch model"><div class="flex items-center"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#ec66f0" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></div></button></span><div id="_r_1lq_" popover="hint" role="tooltip" hidden="" class="fixed inset-s-[calc(anchor(center)+var(--oai-anchor-align-offset,0px))] inset-e-auto top-[calc(anchor(bottom)+var(--oai-anchor-side-offset,var(--spacing)))] bottom-auto h-fit -translate-x-1/2 [position-try-fallbacks:flip-block] flex flex-col overflow-visible bg-transparent z-50 [inset-inline:auto]! translate-none! [position-area:span-all]" style="--oai-anchor-align-offset: initial; --oai-anchor-side-offset: initial; position-anchor: --reaction-_r_1lp_;"></div><button aria-describedby="_r_1lq_" interestfor="_r_1lq_" type="button" class="interactive-button text-token-text-secondary touch:w-10 relative flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg" aria-label="React" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="_r_1lp_" data-state="closed" data-testid="message-reaction-button" style="anchor-name: --reaction-_r_1lp_;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-07247886.svg#c6db2f" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button><div id="_r_1lp_" popover="auto" hidden="" class="fixed inset-s-[calc(anchor(start)+var(--oai-anchor-align-offset,calc(-1*var(--spacing))))] inset-e-auto top-auto bottom-[calc(anchor(top)+var(--oai-anchor-side-offset,var(--spacing)))] h-fit [position-try-fallbacks:flip-block,flip